The
constants of the paper are built from $c_3$ and from the second value
$\kappa(\tfrac15)=\tfrac75+\tfrac35\log_23-\log_25$:
\begin{equation} \begin{aligned}
  \lambda&\ :=\ 1+5\,\kappa(\tfrac15)\ =\ 8+3\log_23-5\log_25,\\
  C&\ :=\ c_3+\frac{\lambda-1}{3} .
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}

\begin{aligned}
  \lambda&\ :=\ 1+5\,\kappa(\tfrac15)\ =\ 8+3\log_23-5\log_25,\\
  C&\ :=\ c_3+\frac{\lambda-1}{3} .
\end{aligned}

For every $p_1\in[\tfrac12,1)$,
  \[
  \begin{aligned}
    &\sup\{R(p):p\text{ a source with largest symbol }p_1\}\\
    &\qquad\qquad=2-p_1-\mathrm H_2(p_1);
  \end{aligned}
  \]
  the supremum is approached but not attained. The final branch of
  Theorem~\ref{thm:main} is therefore best possible.

For every source with $n\ge2$ symbols, $R<p_1+C$. In particular the
first \textup{(}$0<p_1<\tfrac14$\textup{)} branch of Theorem~\ref{thm:main}
holds \textup{(}$p_1<\tfrac12$ forces $n\ge3$\textup{)}.

\textbf{(iii)} Combining (i) and (ii) with the two-level expansion \eqref{eq:2level}
(Lemma~\ref{lem:rec} applied at the root and at $\rho$'s root), the requirement
$R\le\Psi$ reduces to $\Delta\le0$, where
\begin{equation} \begin{split}
  \Delta\ :=\ &2-2p_1+2A-p_2-\mathrm H\bigl(p_1,p_2,A{-}p_2,s{-}A\bigr)\\
  &+p_{m+1}-C\,(p_1+A).
\end{split}
\end{equation}

\begin{split}
  \Delta\ :=\ &2-2p_1+2A-p_2-\mathrm H\bigl(p_1,p_2,A{-}p_2,s{-}A\bigr)\\
  &+p_{m+1}-C\,(p_1+A).
\end{split}

Two exact values anchor our bounds: since $\mathrm H_2(\tfrac13)=\log_23-\tfrac23$,
\[
\begin{aligned}
  \tilde B(\tfrac13)\ &=\ 2-\log_23+\tfrac{C}{3}\ =\ 0.458410\ldots,\\
  \tilde B(\tfrac12)\ &=\ \tfrac{1+C}{2}\ =\ K\ \ \text{exactly};
\end{aligned}
\]
and $\tilde B$ is strictly increasing on $[\tfrac13,\tfrac12]$:
\begin{equation} \tilde B'(x)\ =\ 1+C-\log_2\tfrac{1-x}{x}\ \ge\ 1+C-\log_22\ =\ C\ >\ 0,
\end{equation}
because $\tfrac{1-x}{x}\le2$ for $x\ge\tfrac13$.

conclusions:
R\ <\ \begin{cases}
  \,W_{\mathrm{iso}}(p_1)\ =\ 1-\mathrm H_2(p_1)+(1-p_1)\,\dfrac{1+C}2,\\
  \qquad \tfrac13\le p_1\le p^*,\\[8pt]
  \,F\bigl(p_1,\tfrac\delta3\bigr)\ =\ \dfrac{5-p_1}{3}
    +\dfrac{2-p_1}{3}\,C\\
  \qquad -\mathrm H\Bigl(p_1,\dfrac{1-2p_1}{3},\dfrac{2-p_1}{3}\Bigr),\\
  \qquad p^*\le p_1<\tfrac12.
  \end{cases}

